{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic","id":1422746,"title":"Tzimisce, Metamorphosis, and Blood Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-09T08:41:53-08:00","id":1422746,"title":"Tzimisce, Metamorphosis, and Blood Magic","content":"Hello everyone! This is a bit of a follow-up on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1365619-path-of-metamorphis-except-you-know-other-disciplines-besides-vicissitude-exist\">this thread</a>, but with a more specific focus. As a side note, there was a ton of interesting discussion in there that I apparently missed, so I may bring up some points from in there in addition to the topic listed in the title. I'm not super interested in gritty mechanical details, I'm more interested in themes and philosophy, but I am primarily operating under (DA)V20 rules in case people wonder.<br /> <br /> I've been a big fan of the Tzimisce and the Path of Metamorphosis for a while now. And I've been contemplating possible Metamorphosist characters I might like to create and play some day down the road. As the reference to the previous thread indicates, one of the things I've thought about a fair bit is how Disciplines other than Vicissitude might contribute to the pursuit of Metamorphosis. And because I've always been a fan of playing magic-users, that has included consideration of the use of Blood Magic as part of the endeavour. I'm somewhat torn on the matter. Putting aside my general fondness for sorcery, I've often seen Blood Magic as a way to try and counteract or overcome the spiritual 'deadness' that is often attributed to the Kindred, explaining their limited access to the Umbra, etc. Looking at Koldunic Sorcery, I found the capacity for the Genius Loci/Way of Spirit to expand the senses of the vampire a good example of transcending the limits of the body; the first dot in Way of Fire providing resistance to Rotschreck also made me think of one of the Coils of the Dragon from VtR.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, a part of me feels like Blood Magic focuses a lot on things that are external to the Vampire practicing it; ritual components, arcane language, connections (possibly even subordination) to spirits, deities, demons, etc. And a part of me wonders if it might not be better, or at least more interesting, to play a Metamorphosist who tends to focus more on internal growth and mastery of the more innate powers of other Disciplines. There is almost nothing that can be accomplished by Blood Magic that cannot be accomplished by some other non-magical Discipline; it may require 6+ dots, but it's almost never off the table entirely. I liked MyWifeIsScary's reference to Valeren, along with Daimonion and Spiritus. Chimerstry is another one I would throw in the list, since at really high levels you go beyond just illusions and into full-blown reality-warping.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I would like to hear peoples' opinions on my rambling, with a focus on these particular questions:<br /> <br /> Do you think Blood Magic is or could be a useful tool for a Vampire seeking Metamorphosis? How?<br /> <br /> Do you think a particular style of Blood Magic (Koldunism, Thaumaturgy, etc.) might be particularly suited to the pursuit of Metamorphosis? Why?<br /> <br /> Are there any other Disciplines that haven't been mentioned which you might see as especially useful for the pursuit of Metamorphosis? Do you have any interesting ideas about how the Disciplines already discussed might be used?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T08:59:19-08:00","id":1422752,"title":"","content":"While Vicissitude may make you the perfect organism, Thaumaturgy is a more realistic path to some kind of enlightenment and higher state of being, with most Thaumaturges actively believing that the process of learning miracles brings them closer to god. Koldunic sorcery may eventually transform you to a spirit (but I think relies too much on the umbra really to grant a balanced approach to becoming closer to divinity)<br /> Necromancy is a pretty shit plan for divinity, but Capadocious is trying. Doesn't seem to be going well for him.<br /> <br /> Magics are more tied to the soul, whilst disciplines are tied to the Beast and the Blood. I'd trust the soul more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-09-2020, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T09:20:16-08:00","id":1422755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422752#post1422752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Vicissitude may make you the perfect organism, Thaumaturgy is a more realistic path to some kind of enlightenment and higher state of being, with most Thaumaturges actively believing that the process of learning miracles brings them closer to god. Koldunic sorcery may eventually transform you to a spirit (but I think relies too much on the umbra really to grant a balanced approach to becoming closer to divinity)<br /> Necromancy is a pretty shit plan for divinity, but Capadocious is trying. Doesn't seem to be going well for him.<br /> <br /> Magics are more tied to the soul, whilst disciplines are tied to the Beast and the Blood. I'd trust the soul more.</div> </div> </div> </div>A part of me definitely prefers the more rationalist approach of Thaumaturgy to the more shamanistic practices of the Koldun. But I've seen a number of posts on these forums claiming that Thaumaturgy has been stripped of most of the more transcendentalist aspects that came with the Hermetic paradigm in favour of a more pragmatic focus on power and efficacy, so I considered it up for debate. Could you possibly recommend sources that discuss Thaumaturgy in more spiritual terms? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Because I have an unhealthy fixation on crossover, the Path of Spirit Manipulation from Thaumaturgy and the Ash Path from Necromancy are arguably some of my favourite bits of Blood Magic, giving the Kindred access to parts of reality from which they are normally excluded. But yeah, that doesn't mean the secret to Enlightenment is hiding in the Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Thanks for popping in btw; only reason I didn't @ you in my first post was because I didn't want you to potentially feel dragged in to the topic :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T09:56:53-08:00","id":1422768,"title":"","content":"The main problem is that the followers of path want to ascend. For most Metamorphosists, physical change precedes spiritual change. Some Tzimisce thinks that soul is connected with body (or that soul is just body summarized). Many of them (Tzimisce) study and practice Vicissitude and/or Protean in order to change body, because that is basis of their ascension. This path favors search for knowledge, including magic, occultism, etc. <u>Ancient vampires</u> are able to achieve this goal using Vicissitude. However, young vampires do not have this power, so they can use their knowledge of magic to achieve <u>their</u> ascension.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it (magic) is useful tool, but not main. The main idea of the path is to change the flesh and through this change your soul. No magic school is required for this. Koldunic way of spirit, does not allow you to change your soul, but no one forbids creation of several new combo-disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T10:12:19-08:00","id":1422771,"title":"","content":"Glad to know I'm the resident theological nutjob.<br /> I don't think you really can strip hermetic thaumaturgy of it's... belief in a higher power. That's like being Christian without believing in God, it's just a fundamental part of the idea. But Tremere can (and probably mostly do) believe in a higher power without getting religious about it. Hermetics can believe God is distant, uncaring, or omnipresent to the point that you don't really need to pay god any mind. That's I think is how Tremere approach him. A read-up on hermeticism has this wonderful tidbit on the nature of good and evil that goes &quot;God is good and man is not God, so man cannot be good&quot;. You can only imagine a Tremere reading this and answering with &quot;So I shouldn't even try to be good!&quot; or, if they're ambitious, &quot;So to be good I need to become God!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Hermeticism is the Optimistic brother of Gnosticism, which is basically the same ideas except reality's a prison. The Setites actively believe they're following in the footsteps of their God Set who challenged reality's jailor. To follow Set (who may just be a Caine analogue honestly), they need Disciplines, they need Akhu (thaumaturgy), and they need to approach closer to godhood without forming chains with the jailor's servants (IE form pacts with Aeons or demons)<br /> <br /> Moving back to Hermeticism and the Tremere, you can kind of see a parallel between the Tremere wanting to cut down on extraneous deities and religious practices and the Setites being very particular about worshiping the wrong thing or taking up demons even though they're a corruption cult. There's certainly differences, and in general the Tremere want you to worship the Pyramid almost as much as Setites want you to revere Set for the sake of your own freedom. But for the most part the belief may just be that the less gods you have, the more you can focus on your personal ascension towards power and divinity. (Assamite sorcerers, in contrast, believe the spirits are actually helping them. Ascend that <b>ladder of heaven</b> baby!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-09-2020, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T10:51:06-08:00","id":1422777,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25408_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25408\" data-vbnamecard=\"25408\">Alphari</a> The entire point of the Path is the problem...? Other than that, yeah, mainstream Metamorphosists focus on physical transformation and Vicissitude, but both the title of this thread and the previous thread linked emphasize that we're interested in discussing beyond that, so all the talk about how Vicissitude alone is good enough for some is kind of irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> \u200b\u200bI was mostly just talking about my reference to your mention of Valeren, lol, but you are good for discussing the philosophies of Hermeticism, Gnosticism, etc., as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Your posts have probably contributed to my interest in the Setites growing more recently.<br /> <br /> I guess the question becomes how you are defining &quot;God&quot; or &quot;Higher Power,&quot; and what you imagine their relationship with the process of Metamorphosis to be. That does still seem to suffer from the problem of a preoccupation with some outside Other rather than the internal condition of the Cainite. But if working with 'God' could eventually result in the achievement of Azhi Dahaka, independent from and not subordinate to that Higher Power in some fashion, then it could be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T10:55:53-08:00","id":1422778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic#post1422746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think Blood Magic is or could be a useful tool for a Vampire seeking Metamorphosis? How?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, blood magic (koldunism and thaumaturgy) are ways to metamorphosis,<br /> this is canon...CANON, caaaanon<br /> <br /> however, you can't exclude vicissitude,<br /> metamorphosis wants ascension in both flesh and soul, flesh (vicissitude), soul (auspex, koldunism, thaumaturgy),<br /> <br /> if you're only concerned by flesh and vicissitude, consider applying to the Cathari church instead<br /> <br /> <br /> now if you're asking about my own take,<br /> in my own head canon, I'd just make thaumaturgy not work,<br /> the vampiric soul is dead, deal with it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 11-09-2020, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T11:18:27-08:00","id":1422786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422778#post1422778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes, blood magic (koldunism and thaumaturgy) are ways to metamorphosis,<br /> this is canon...CANON, caaaanon</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite me some sources! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Please tell me where they put a step-by-step roadmap to Metamorphosis in writing that includes the necessary conditions, and lists the ways in which Blood Magic can help you concretely achieve that goal.<br /> <br /> I believe the closest thing there is to a hard source on &quot;what&quot; Metamorphosis might actually look like is in the Revised Tzimisce Clanbook, but I do not recall it making any definite claims about the efficacy of Blood Magic in achieving that end. That and the Eldest supposedly achieving it in &quot;Crucible of God,&quot; but that's pretty outside the purview of a regular Metamorphosist.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, AFAIK what is &quot;CANON, caaaanon,&quot; is that many Metamorphosists are Blood Magic practitioners, and that they <b>believe in-character</b> that Blood Magic is helpful in achieving it.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just a different attitude about Metamorphosis, but while I agree 100% with the importance of both physical and spiritual transformation, I strongly oppose the idea that Vicissitude must be a necessary condition. I'm also skeptical/critical of absolute declarations about the &quot;deadness&quot; of the vampiric soul. But I absolutely asked for your take, and I appreciate you offering some input <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T11:25:01-08:00","id":1422787,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce don't really care about any entities other than themselves (which is not to say Vampires generally aren't like that as well, its just Tzimisce exemply this the most). The fundamental aspect of this path is the improvement of Vicissitude and likewise by that alone, improving themselves by all means to gain more insight into the physical side of things. They're not looking for God(s) or anything beyond transcending themselves personally through the body alone. The Tzimisce is essentially a clan of biologists, studying the biomechanics of flesh, bone, chitin and cartilage matter of different beings when their not flesh-crafting themselves personally.<br /> <br /> They take animals that are nothing like- say a centipede and a squirrel, fusing them together and giving them Vitae to make some sort of beast. They kidnap random humans to test on the body with such things folding over the head skin over the captive's ears with trying to gain insight of how the subject reacts psychologically. They sneak inside peoples homes at random and switch out body parts from other unfortunate test subjects, to then have ghouls in on the experiment record and observe the results of the reaction from the people suddenly found with new limbs come morning.<br /> <br /> The highest facet of Metamorphical is exhibited in The Eldest when after many centuries of close calls of almost being destroyed, he came to the New World and settled in the sewer systems of NYC where he literally transcended into a entity higher than itself. It absorbed multiple other Kindred, its childer- any unfortunate to happen in the near abandoned section where The Eldest found itself into its own being; to a point where The Eldest was a hive-mind of multiple entities at once; Apotheosis. That is the path of Metamorphosis basically and I don't know how other Disciplines (beside &quot;Protean&quot;, but that's more turning into or shifting into animals than manipulating biological processes into unknown and horrifying ways unexplainable by nature) that can tie into this philosophy more than Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> Even with all this in mind, why there is some predication that Tzimisce can't study or train other disciplines than Vicissitude- you can. It's just that Vicissitude was the sole reason of why Metamorphosis as a philosophy came about in the first place. However that's not to say you can't use other Disciplines to help you with your experimentations. At its root, its a path to gain knowledge. None of the moral guidelines of the Path say you HAVE to only use Vicissitude to gain biological insight. If you wish to use Blood Magic as a supplement to gain results to record for your experiment, do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-09-2020, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T11:27:40-08:00","id":1422788,"title":"","content":"Those spiritual disciplines are almost sure ways of becoming something other than the vampire state. There are genuine mechanical powers for -stop being a vampire- among them. Spiritus can become spirits, Valeren can have you detach from the mortal coil (I can't remember which particular book this was) Diamonion... well, like, it's either Valeren's western brother or it's evil twin or... some editions have posited a relationship between the two. It doesn't explicitly have a power for any form of ascension, but Quite honestly I think most of Diamonion at 7+ is just wrong and should better carry the themes of the last 6 levels; becoming a demon. <br /> <br /> However, whilst you're changing into something else, I'm not sure if you're really changing into something better by becoming energy and floating off. Spiritus seems the weakest option out of the three, as you can become get lost as a spirit at only 6th or 7th level, but that still qualifies as 'metamorphosis' I think. Valeren's 'escape' is a higher level power, and I would match Diamonion's 'escape' at the same level. Diamonion 6's ability to invest in yourself is perhaps, a very good power for the idea of immediate 'metamorphosis'; you can just keep buying new and spectacular powers with it and push yourself beyond the perceived perception of what a vampire is with that power: Immunity to fire, a beast you have chained yourself, more beauty, more strength, permanent wealth... <br /> <br /> <br /> Back to Sorcery. <br /> There's a really, really fun power in rites of the blood for New Age sorcerers. You get a cult, have them drink the coolaid, and experience the fragments of their soul. With very nice benefits. This could spur you to become a serial mass-killer in the name of metamorphosis. However, I do wonder if the behavious concerning this power really fits 'The path of metamorphosis'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:33:28-08:00","id":1422806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The entire point of the Path is the problem...? </div> </div> </div>This is a problem for magical ascension. Shakalaka wrote what I wanted to write to you earlier. The whole idea of Metamorphosis is to achieve a new form of existence through the control of the flesh by your will/soul. Try to be inspired by [Eldest] or mage.<br /> This path does not work well with other disciplines or methods:<ul><li>Anarchs Ritual can be a source of inspiration for you and your character.<i> But you need to eat a rare anarch who knows this ritual.</i></li> <li>Blood magic requires complex rituals and often does not allow you to change your essence.</li> <li>Spiritus / Daimonion - The first discipline can hypothetically change you, but that's not what metamorphs need. Being spirit has its own problems, and there will be more problems... The second is clearly not what you want, since this discipline is not about changing the flesh.</li> <li>Most other disciplines and blood magics do not specialize in this.</li> </ul>About Vicissitude: Path \u0430depts believe that Vicissitude is key to achieving &quot;new form.&quot; Technically, path dont required to use Vicissitude, but this discipline is much more useful than others.<u><i> This path was created by Tzimisce.</i></u><br /> <br /> PS: Do you want to know more about path of assaku? <span style=\"font-size:10px\">First dot in Vicissitude is free.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:35:23-08:00","id":1422807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422786#post1422786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cite me some sources! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Please tell me where they put a step-by-step roadmap to Metamorphosis in writing that includes the necessary conditions, and lists the ways in which Blood Magic can help you concretely achieve that goal.<br /> <br /> I believe the closest thing there is to a hard source on &quot;what&quot; Metamorphosis might actually look like is in the Revised Tzimisce Clanbook, but I do not recall it making any definite claims about the efficacy of Blood Magic in achieving that end. That and the Eldest supposedly achieving it in &quot;Crucible of God,&quot; but that's pretty outside the purview of a regular Metamorphosist.</div> </div> </div> </div>it says in the corebook that they value both thaumaturgy and auspex<br /> <br /> I don't know about about the Tzimisce clanbook, it sounded more like metamorphosists &quot;on their way&quot; to metamorphosis,<br /> not masters of metamorphosis<br /> <br /> both masters, Tzimisce himself and Velya have koldunism<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is definitely a way to break the limits of vampirism, but it's not enough,<br /> it breaks the stasis of the body, but you still sleep during the day, you still burn under sunlight, and you're still limited to feeding on blood (at least at leve 9, I'm not sure if [Tzimisce] has found a counter to those)<br /> <br /> the necessity of thaumaturgy or koldunism to reach the highest point is obvious in my opinion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:40:33-08:00","id":1422810,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> \u200bI can agree that the transformative nature of Vicissitude served to inspire the Tzimisce to develop the Path of Metamorphosis, but the argument that Vicissitude is necessarily the best or most important tool for the job doesn't follow from that. I also reject the conception of the Tzimisce as predominantly biologists, primarily or exclusively concerned with physical evolution. I have been very inspired by the example of the Eldest in that regard, but I don't consider it the end-all-be-all approach. One of the coolest things about the concept of Metamorphosis is that each individual Metamorphosists endeavour will likely be somewhat unique, and the transcendent Thing that they are trying to become in the process is likely to be similarly unique as well. Arguably my favourite models for what Metamorphosis could look like, however, is the Vicissitude 6/Way of Spirit 6 power &quot;Becoming Kupala,&quot; becoming both a physical and spiritual presence within your domain, and then taking things further from there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I definitely agree that &quot;just becoming a spirit&quot; as a way to &quot;escape&quot; vampirism doesn't seem appropriate to me; the idea is to become something MORE, not just something different. That's why I tend to be interested in both the physical evolution and spiritual development sides of Metamorphosis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I think I may recall the ritual you mention and remember being quite intrigued by it, lol.<br /> <br /> \u200bP.S. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> But again, AFAIK what that is describing is an in-character opinion, not a mechanically-objective fact about the end goal of the Path. And unless I remember wrong, the stuff lined out in TzRev *is* described as &quot;what Azhi Dakaka should look like, if you wanna put it in-game.&quot; I just happen to agree it's a bad depiction, lol.<br /> <br /> And AFAIK Velya is explicitly noted as failing on the Path, due to his attempts to save his childe Elaine. Again, the Eldest is our only possible &quot;canon&quot; example of what Azhi Dahaka might look like, and being shrouded in Antediluvian mystery makes most assumptions about how It did it sketchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 11-09-2020, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:59:49-08:00","id":1422813,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce on the Path of Metamorphosis don't care about spiritual development or dealing with Umbrood, they care about changing biomechanics; research of the scientific processes of life, death, and the locomotives inbetween. The level 2 sin of Metamorphosis is <i>&quot;Neglecting to alter one's own <b>body</b>&quot;</i>, with the following Rationale for this since being: <i>&quot;<b>Physical</b> change must be attained before any more significant metamorphosis&quot;</i>. The fact that this sin is so low (lower being more severe) tells that a Tzimisce on the Path of Metamorphosis isn't going to waste time on such Disciplines that broaches the Middle-Umbra significantly (from what I sparse of what you want for whatever character your developing). Yes, its not to say they CAN'T dabble such Disciplines when not versing in the Path of Metamorphosis on some time set aside- or maybe use such Disciplines as aides to further a particular point of research- but that's not the modus operandi of the Path as a whole.<br /> <br /> It came about from Vicissitude as a way of thought thereafter and trying to remove this Discipline outright or make it not important to this Path is nonsensical to the dynamic it was shaped around. If your a fan of the Path of Metamorphosis as you say, you'll already know all of this. If you want to play Tzimisce with a heightened focus on Blood Magic alone or with more importance steeped to that, you can always go for the &quot;Old&quot; Clan Tzimisce. Their literally a faction of the Tzimisce who split of from the main branch because they were adverse to Vicissitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-09-2020, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T15:32:09-08:00","id":1422831,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> (and anyone else on the &quot;Metamorphosis is all about biology&quot; train)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Tzimisce Rev. p.52</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>most</b> Metamorphosists, physical change precedes spiritual change... Others ignore the physical element and, instead, seek to exploit the peculiar nature of undeath. Some such Metamorphosists feed only on their fellow Cainites, believing that an aversion to mortal blood is a sign of metaphysical superiority. Some believe that following certain precepts, such as \u201clearn the characteristics of all stages of life and death,\u201d will lead them to a reward similar to that mythic Golconda.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Core p.332</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many Metamorphosists also specialize Academics in areas such as philosophy and theology in hopes of uncovering secrets unexplored in larger fields of study.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DAV20 Core p.133</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Spirit regard the flesh as nearly inconsequential, a tool to aid them in the refinement of their souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>*ahem*<br /> <br /> But, I will be fair to you lot:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast p.69</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As discussed previously, Vicissitude is an absolute requirement of this path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just say &quot;ick&quot; in response.<br /> <br /> And I want to be very clear that I mean this in all seriousness, and I am not trying to troll you lot, but you are almost certainly going to believe I am:<br /> <br /> In both V20's Path (level 2 sin) and DAV20's Road (level 1 sin), the words are &quot;alter one's own body.&quot; Not &quot;alter one's body into a transhuman entity.&quot; &quot;Alter one's own body.&quot; Piercings alter one's body. Tattoos alter one's body. Shaving one's hair alters one's body. If you accept the idea that there are more approaches to Metamorphosis than biology, a position that I believe I have provided evidence for above, then it is possible to understand how altering one's body in a vast assortment of ways could be used to &quot;alter one's soul.&quot; There is no mechanically-written mention of how Vicissitude &quot;alters the soul&quot; of a Metamorphosist, yet it is presumed to be possible by fans of the Path; why is the notion that things other than Vicissitude, like new experiences or an expanded consciousness, are not also capable of &quot;altering the soul&quot; in meaningful ways?<br /> <br /> It's not really appropriate for the mainstream Road/Path, but I had an idea for an outcast Tzimisce that is influenced by Metamorphosist philosophy but hasn't abandoned Humanity (or perhaps has adopted a more Humanity-tolerant deviation) where they use Vicissitude to effectively hide amongst human society and study them.<br /> <br /> But then, the Dracon is one of my all-time favourite Tzimisce, and his being all about changing the world and society around him as much as his own form was a big part of what got me interested in the Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 11-09-2020, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T16:12:20-08:00","id":1422841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no mechanically-written mention of how Vicissitude &quot;alters the <i><b>soul</b></i>&quot; of a Metamorphosist, yet it is presumed to be possible by fans of the Path</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because that's not what anyone (&quot;lot&quot; as you deign it, very quaint..) in this thread responding to has argued. Vicissitude isn't about altering the soul or any such things, its about the physical and that's what the Path of Metamorphosis espouses. DAV20 doesn't specifically mention adjective, but the Path Metamorphosis- not the Road- entails that you have to change your physical self as a Rationale. Again- Metamorphosis is a way of thought that came from state of Vicissitude and the ability it has.<br /> <br /> To discuss you other ideal- you can't be influenced by Metamorphosist thought or practice it and still have semblances of broaching the facet of Humanity. Its so alien from Humanity that its ridiculous to think Tzimisce would search for someone to embrace like that in the first place, they go for humans already very cold or lacking the common qualities that assemble traits specific to things that would make them fringe on Humanity post embrace. Such Tzimisce who clung to Humanity would probably be destroyed by their sires. Vampires by fiat already can hide amongst human society very well considering almost all Vampires live in cities.. where y'know, the highest concentration of humans are. A Tzimisce doesn't need Vicissitude for hiding, it needs it for shaping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T16:31:21-08:00","id":1422844,"title":"","content":"So I cite like three sources supporting my assertion, and you skirt around it by cherry-picking the word &quot;soul&quot; like I didn't just provide a quote about how mainstream Metamorphosist philosophy posits physical change as a predecessor to <b>spiritual change</b>.<br /> <br /> And again, I'm not rejecting the importance of physical transformation in Metamorphosis, I'm rejecting the claim that spiritual evolution is irrelevant. Which is, again, a position that I've backed up with multiple citations.<br /> <br /> Cite your sources, or step out please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T17:14:31-08:00","id":1422848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clan Book Tzimisce, pg. 29</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Metamorphosists possess a scientific bent, seeking enlightenment through any number of unholy experiments on mortal and vampire alike. By performing research on life, a vampire can better understand unlife; by performing research on unlife, a vampire can learn enough to trascend that state.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bulk of Tzimisce on Metamorphosis are delving into biological science, whether dead or undead. Most of their experimentation in regards to gaining knowledge is gaining insight on the different processes how biology works or the difference of stimuli between reactions. They're not going to be bothered with Spirits or studying Umbra because it has nothing to do with themselves or will it do anything improve their bodies. Spirits in WoD universe are &quot;alive&quot; and made of ephemera, they aren't dead.<br /> <br /> When a Path adherant of Metamorphosis wants to study stuff that are alive, they are going to focus on either humans, animals, or insects in the physical realm of things. The 1st quote you even lob, you specifically bold the word &quot;most&quot; signaling that Tzimisce on Metamorphosis thereafter in the blurb that focus on Spirit matters aren't the norm- so it isn't mainstream as you clammer for. Even when further analyzing the quote, no where does it mention Spirits for that matter, rather undeath and feeding on other kindred, that's it. If anything, if a Tzimisce wants to further learn things about death as Metamorphosis says they should, it would make more sense to learn Necromancy to simply observe and study Wraiths. Almost all the Spirits from the Middle and High Umbra were never human and never even experienced the physical aspects of &quot;life&quot;. Yes, they are &quot;alive&quot;, but only in a ephemerical manner and were never mortal- so they can't give any insights to Tzimisce. Then again, asking for knowledge would be breach of the Path morality in the first place.<br /> <br /> Again, Metamorphosists (the majority) aren't seeking spirit change. They're seeking physical metamorphosis. That's what things like Vicissitude and Protean are for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Also you want quotes of contestation to your own? I looked into the last book you referenced and found these:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast, pg. 69</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Common Abilities: </b>Metamorphosis relies on a Canite's <b>scientific</b> and <i><b>medical</b></i> education. Characters must have good scores in Academics (something that what was in your previous quote, but Academics could be almost anything its very broad), <b>Medicine</b>, Occult and <b>Science</b> in order to understand even a fraction of what goes on around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metamorphosists are using mostly science and studying results from that to gain insights. They aren't going to be focused on Spirit or Blood Magic matters above Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast, pg. 68</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some senses, this path is not so much a &quot;spiritual&quot; guide as a recipe for physical and mental development. The soul, while <b>acknowledged</b> to exist, is ultimately a building block in the whole of vampiric being. <i><b>It should be perserved, certainly not lost, but not cultivated to the exclusion of all else, either</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give you that yes, Metamorphosists give some importance to the soul, but it is merely acknowledgment. Followers of the path see it as only a building block to aide insight, but the path wants more things inline with the Physical than all else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast, pg. 68</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are common to all metamorphosists and typically involve mastering the Vicissitude Discipline to level 4 while simultaneously purging one's self of human sentiment (raising Conviction to atleast 3).</div> </div> </div> </div>As we see, Vicissitude is a VERY important aspect of Metamorphosism. To be even credible in it or say you practice it to its letter, you need to &quot;shape&quot; up (pun intended) your Vicissitude. Where does this path claims to have anything to do with Blood Magic is more important than Vicissitude? Almost nowhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast, pg 67</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Atomic Age and beyond have likewise been fruitful. Advances in <b>human science</b> provide <i><b>parallels or precursors</b></i> for the work of metamorphosists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here in the History section of Metamorphosist outright states that the sciences were either parallels or even <i>precursors</i> of Metamorphosis thought, signaling that yes, followers of this path are proto-biologists focused on the physical aspects of the processes of life and death- biomechanics. Little importance is steeped in Spiritualism. Not to say NO aspects aren't a part to help with research, but it isn't primary. Vicissitude is the primary discipline where Metamorphosis was wrought from to form a way of thought. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-09-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T19:03:35-08:00","id":1422858,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> , I did in fact see those quotes when digging up the ones that supported my position. You took the time to get offended by my use of the word &quot;lot,&quot; so you had to have read the part that I acknowledged that &quot;Chaining the Beast&quot; was the exception that did undisputedly place Vicissitude at the centre of Metamorphosist practice. So you're bringing up one source that I have already acknowledged, and countered with three more, including one which is very clear that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Tzimisce Rev. p.52</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>For most Metamorphosists, physical change precedes spiritual change.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422844#post1422844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>And again, I'm not rejecting the importance of physical transformation in Metamorphosis, I'm rejecting the claim that spiritual evolution is irrelevant. Which is, again, a position that I've backed up with multiple citations.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Simply proving that physiology and science are important doesn't matter, because I agree with that position. But the idea that it is the defining feature of the Path is ridiculous. I would have to go back and check to be sure, but I'm pretty sure even &quot;Chaining the Beast&quot; acknowledges that Koldunism was a major component of early Metamorphosist philosophy. And Azhi Dahaka is often compared to Nirvana.<br /> <br /> So unless you have another source to pull out that contends that Vicissitude is the end-all of Metamorphosis, or that spirituality is unimportant to Metamorphosis, please vacate my thread you darn Asakku :P<br /> <br /> P.S. for the work of scientists to be a &quot;precursor&quot; to Metamorphosist work is to say that is came BEFORE the Metamorphosists; what they're trying to say is that modern science opens up new avenues for Metamorphosist research, not that Metamorphisists were all proto-biologists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 11-09-2020, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T19:45:41-08:00","id":1422863,"title":"","content":"The revised quote you use as some sort of proof for saying spiritualism is more important than physical matters is more of your own confusion of the convention of the sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Tzimisce Rev. p.52</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>most</b> Metamorphosists, physical change <b>precedes</b> spiritual change... Others ignore the physical element and, instead, seek to exploit the peculiar nature of undeath. Some such Metamorphosists feed only on their fellow Cainites, believing that an aversion to mortal blood is a sign of metaphysical superiority. Some believe that following certain precepts, such as \u201clearn the characteristics of all stages of life and death,\u201d will lead them to a reward similar to that mythic Golconda.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key word here being MOST and PRECEDES.. The majority of Tzimisce see physical change as a PRECEDE, meaning that studying matters of the physical would deign to be first over the latter of spiritual change. I can infer this because after this sentence it goes on by talking about the few Tzimisce WHO IGNORE the physical element and seek insight into undeath instead. They aren't the norm by this analysis and breakdown. Even then if their going down that path and going to use some form of Blood Magic to gain insights into undeath, their going to be doing Necromancy to be perfectly honest. That's where the insights of death truly are, not the Middle Umbra because that's the spirit wilds where living ephemereal entities live and not the High Umbra, because that's too where ephemereal entities exist. They are living, not dead.<br /> <br /> And no, Chaining the Beast has NOTHING on Koldunism now that I have fully read the passage. To even nip this thread in the butt, the second to last bullet of the Ethics part of the Path of Metamorphosis;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast, pg 66</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One should alter and augment one's body. Changing the flesh might pave the way toward changing the <b>soul.</b> As without, so within. While altering one's flesh in and of itself does not lead to enlightenment, the act of experiencing the <b>the physical world through a different body-lens can in turn lead to innovative ways of thinking - or unthinking, as the case may be.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is something even <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25408_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25408\" data-vbnamecard=\"25408\">Alphari</a> has said before previously in this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a problem for magical ascension. Shakalaka wrote what I wanted to write to you earlier. The whole idea of Metamorphosis is to achieve a new form of existence through the control of the flesh by your will/soul. Try to be inspired by [Eldest] or mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there, Vicissitude by followers Metamorphosis see it as the way to mold the soul through physical change and experimentation. Their not going to waste time with the Spirit disciplines/blood magic you want so badly. If they need to transcend by any means inline with Metamorphosis that isn't physical, that's what Auspex is for at the very best and its a Discipline they start with at embrace. Also calling me an Asakku?<br /> <br /> Just admit you want your character concept to be an &quot;Old&quot; Clan Tzimisce and be done with it. The whole reason for them to break off was to not be involved with Vicissitude and study something else. I don't know what path &quot;Old&quot; Clan Tzimisce go by, but just nab that instead. They're not going to want to go with Metamorphosis at all because that Path dictates you have to be proficient in it to even be considered of following it; the entire fiat of &quot;Old&quot; Clan Tzimisce is hating and having a distaste for this Discipline. Site me a source anywhere where it says Koldunism is distinctly needed for Metamorphosis at all. The Preferred Disciplines portion of the book only referenced a minimum of Vicissitude 4 and the other disciplines beside that were Animalism, Auspex, and Fortitude. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> PSS, you also leave out the parallel part in the quote from Chaining the Beasts, which means many of the work of the Metamorphosists were congruent or essentially compatible with biological knowledge the humans caught up to that the Tzimisce already knew. Though it can be agreed that some of the avenues you mentioned also helped in some aspects Metamorphosists missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-09-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T20:18:11-08:00","id":1422865,"title":"","content":"I'm not confused by the word &quot;precede&quot; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> . It means &quot;to come before,&quot; as in &quot;Metamorphosists are interested in physical transformation because it <b>precedes</b> the spiritual transformation that is necessary for Azhi Dahaka.&quot;<br /> <br /> And again, MOST is all I need. If there are SOME Metamorphosists that consider spiritual evolution to be an important part of Metamorphosis, then I am correct. YOU are the one trying to argue that spiritual matters are irrelevant to the Path at large, and you are the one with less sources to support your position.<br /> <br /> Plus, your own quotes helps my case:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Tzimisce Rev. p.52</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Others ignore the physical element and, instead, seek to exploit the peculiar nature of undeath.</b> Some such Metamorphosists feed only on their fellow Cainites, believing that an aversion to mortal blood is a sign of <b>metaphysical</b> superiority. <b>Some believe that following certain precepts, such as \u201clearn the characteristics of all stages of life and death,\u201d will lead them to a reward similar to that mythic Golconda.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaining the Beast, p.66</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>While altering one's flesh in and of itself does not lead to enlightenment, the act of <b>experiencing</b> the the physical world through a different body-lens can in turn lead to <b>innovative ways of thinking</b> - or unthinking, as the case may be.<br /> </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's about new experiences and perceptions, which is why changes to the body that are not necessarily produced via Vicissitude are reasonable to consider.<br /> <br /> Also, please stop bringing up the Old Clan. Stop conflating &quot;Vicissitude is not the centre of the universe&quot; with &quot;Ew, I hate Vicissitude.&quot; It's an uncharitable distortion of my position.<br /> <br /> One of the sources that I read linked koldunism with Metamorphosis, but I'm willing to concede I was wrong about it being in &quot;Chaining the Beast.&quot;<br /> <br /> And again, I've provided three sources disproving the idea that physical transformation is the sole preoccupation of Metamorphosists, so quoting someone who spoke up before I provided said evidence is irrelevant, and dragging more points out of the one source I have already acknowledged to be in agreement with your position is redundant.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to concede that the questions I opened this thread with technically left room for the response &quot;No, no Discipline except Vicissitude is useful for Metamorphosis,&quot; so you're not derailing the topic by stating your opinion. But your opinion has been stated, discussed, and you are no longer adding new material to the discussion, just repeating the same points. If you want to make your own thread discussing all the reasons you think that Metamorphosis is or should be all about Vicissitude, then I invite you to do so, but at this point you are dragging things off-topic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T20:24:42-08:00","id":1422867,"title":"","content":"For a possible new conversation prompt, on the relationship between physical and spiritual transformation, Valeren literally causes you to grow a third eye <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T21:05:32-08:00","id":1422869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">changes to the body that are not necessarily produced via Vicissitude</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which Animalism and Auspex are already for. The quote you bring up says about experiencing things in the <i>physical</i> world. Spirits and the Middle and High Umbra (the things you want involved with Metamorphosis) aren't of the physical world at all. I'd say if any other disciplines that would complement Metamorphosis other than Vicissitude would be Protean, Serpentis, Abombwe, and Visceratika for its shape-shifting abilities. Protean for physical inhuman strength, Celerity for inhuman speed, Fortitude for inhuman endurance, Flight.. for well, flight (however a Metamorphosis path user will learn that, IDK. Maybe diablerie then improve from there). Now what do all these Disciplines all have in common? They're all physical and broach the tenants Metamorphosis wants. There it is- the other Disciplines that could help in gaining further conviction in Metamorphosis as you change more and more into something.. else for transcendence (like we see what [The Eldest] had done in NYC).<br /> <br /> The sources I got is just from one book, but one book can have many sources to draw from. Why can't I take from that (especially when this book is the one that is imperatively dealing with Paths in the first place)? If you say you agree with Chains of the Beasts then you agree with this citation from the book (remember, your the one who asked for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />);<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chain the Beast, pg.66</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One should alter and augment one's body. Changing the flesh might pave the way toward changing the soul. As without, so within. While altering one's flesh in and of itself does not lead to enlightenment, the act of experiencing the the physical world through a different body-lens can in turn lead to innovative ways of thinking - or unthinking, as the case may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually now that I look at your post, you bring it too. But mysteriously you leave out this part for whatever reason: <i><b>&quot;One should alter and augment one's body. Changing the flesh might pave the way toward changing the soul.&quot;</b></i> Oh and I've given plenty of counter sources in return; also me mentioning <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25408_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25408\" data-vbnamecard=\"25408\">Alphari</a> IS relevant because his reasoning is exactly inline with the book says, suggesting he has read it before at some point. That's why I brought him up after mentioning that pg.66 quote.<br /> <br /> Also while its true that you've shown Metamorphosists focus on other things, its still not the norm from the main focus of Vicissitude. Even then if they would be looking at different avenues, they'll get into looking to the previous Disciplines I mentioned. Spiritualist Blood Magic? Not so much. If anything is to do with the soul or spiritualism for a Metamorphosis as hammered again and again in this thread, they're going to be looking for the Physical to influence the Soul, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> You're right about one thing and made me realize one thing: Vicissitude isn't the end-all for advancing Metamorphosis- I thank you for that honestly. There are many Disciplines that can aide in experimentation, insight, and general knowledge for this Path as I referenced them specifically before as possible options. The fundamental thing you have to realize is that Vicissitude was the reason for Metamorphosis even being a thing as we know it to begin with however and is very important; its to as &quot;close&quot; to &quot;be-all&quot; as you can get for this philosophy, but certainly not the &quot;end-all&quot; to all &quot;means&quot; to advance in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-10-2020, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T01:36:50-08:00","id":1422885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422831#post1422831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a><br /> In both V20's Path (level 2 sin) and DAV20's Road (level 1 sin), the words are &quot;alter one's own body.&quot; Not &quot;alter one's body into a transhuman entity.&quot; &quot;Alter one's own body.&quot; Piercings alter one's body. Tattoos alter one's body. Shaving one's hair alters one's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something tells me that piercings and tattoos are not about this path.<br /> <u><i>One should alter and augment one's body - changing the flesh may pave the way toward changing the soul.</i></u> (V20) I think... this is not enough to change your hair style or paint your nails, this is not evolution path.<br /> <i><u>Preferred Disciplines: The Tzimisce Metamorphosists favor attention to their unique powers of Vicissitude. Thaumaturgy and Auspex are also highly prized.</u></i> In other words, if you are Tzimisce, you will use your discipline and then try to reach Azhi Dahaka.<br /> <br /> The main idea is evolution of Cainite. Path of Metamorphosis is creation of clan that changes its flesh.<br /> <u><i>Azi Dahaka: Persian name of the three-headed dragon of the demon Ahriman. To the Tzimisce, it is the Metamorphosist's Holy Grail, an enlightened and ultimate state of being, possibly brought on by extensive use of Vicissitude</i></u> (V20 LoC)<br /> <br /> One should alter and augment one\u2019s body \u2014 changing the flesh may pave the way toward changing the soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422831#post1422831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a><br /> There is no mechanically-written mention of how Vicissitude &quot;alters the soul&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Assaku? Loss of humanity and new desire to make people-chair or people-horse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422831#post1422831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a><br /> Tzimisce that is influenced by Metamorphosist philosophy but hasn't abandoned Humanity<br /> they use Vicissitude to effectively hide amongst human society and study them.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Followers of the Path of Metamorphosis are truly some of the most alien creatures any Kindred could meet. Metamorphosists are cold, utterly inhuman, and exactingly scientific. Their concerns are metaphysical rather than ethical, and it is precisely this frame of mind that leads many to believe that the Metamorphosists have literally begun their transformation into something else. Some take this a step further by altering their flesh in various means until they no longer have a recognizable gender or look even remotely human.</i><br /> <u>Virtues: Conviction and Instinct</u><br /> <br /> It seems to me that the followers of the path do not want to be human.<br /> <br /> Edited: Hmm ... I didn't notice this second page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 11-10-2020, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T04:31:47-08:00","id":1422894,"title":"","content":"Barring access to high level Disciplines, Blood Magic would be the way to go.<br /> <br /> Since most characters will not have access to high level Disciplines, developing Paths of Thaumaturgy would work. You have Biothaumaturgical Experimentation, for one. That works for 'altering the body' (unless you can't use it on yourself), but what about transcending other limits?<br /> <br /> I could see a Metamorphosist developing Paths that allowed longer times between feeding (or increasing what you get from feeding), reducing rolls for Frenzy and Roetschreck, allowing daytime activity to not be capped by Morality... Really, I see more opportunity for Metamorphosis when you get past Vicissitude. I liked V20 Tal'Mahe'Ra that had the Old Clan imply that Vicissitude was a crutch set up by the Eldest, and that the Eldest also fell into the trap of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T05:26:29-08:00","id":1422897,"title":"","content":"You do know that Disciplines (the type of you get depending on your clan) are something you at least get in Embrace, right? The most complete part of Vicissitude is when you fully get up to 3 dot portion where your basically set to fully manipulate all parts of a biological matter and viscera for study; right before getting to level 4 of Vicissitude, the target of where the Ethics of Metamorphosis espouses you need to get to this competency to be considered following the path. 1-4 of Vicissitude isn't HIGH whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Biothaumaturgical Thaumaturgy is certainly a Path of Blood Magic that could help in Metamorphosis, but not that much considering Vicissitude already covers half of the aforementioned Path in only 3 dots- it would be redundant to have both. Vicissitude is also something Tzimisce start with (unless again, you make some sort of Old Clan character- even then you have to LEARN Thaumaturgy, its not something you just get from embrace), so developing Vicissitude that you already have rationally makes more sense.<br /> <br /> Even then the path you mention is a Blackhand Path- y'know the sect where the OLD CLAN is in. Its very unlikely they're going to teach or allow a regular Tzimisce to gain access to it (never mind that Metamorphosis all knowledges you have to learn for yourself). The way I read it further, it seems the Path you suggest is more for general members who aren't Tzimisce because the dots of it are already things Tzimisce can already do. They can already experiment on animals, humans, and supernatural creatures (biological matter, inert non-biological matter such as Golems by some such margin, not so much) off that bat with Vicissitude with simple fleshcraft, level 2 of the Discipline.. That doesn't seem very high level at all. Though Biothaumaturgy could very much be a good supplement to aide in Metamorposis... but its still quite redundant to have when we compare Vicissitude over it...<br /> <br /> And gain, it seems most people who keep saying or imply Vicissitude isn't important to the Path seem to have an Old Clan slant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-10-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T09:57:25-08:00","id":1422919,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11149\" data-vbnamecard=\"11149\">PJ123</a> Thank you for bothering to respect the premise of the thread.<br /> <br /> Apparently it's broken as hell, but I rather liked the Path of Focused Will as an &quot;internal improvement&quot; Path. I haven't looked at Biothaumaturgy much, but it seems like it might open options that might otherwise not be available to Vicissitude until higher levels, or might be useful for someone interested in the Path that doesn't otherwise have access to Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> To the extent that I like the way World of Darkness generally makes a giant mysterious mess of their lore and cosmology, I liked the take in V20's Black Hand book. But I ultimately disagree with it, to at least some extent. I'm not especially fond of Vicissitude-as-a-trap as a theory. The closest that I generally like to come is that almost any exposure to Vicissitude involves coming into contact with Tzimisce blood, which connects you to the Eldest through Its power of Vicissitude. But as other threads have pointed out, Antediluvians as a rule are capable of messing people up on a global scale, especially their descendants, so the Eldest having one particular avenue for doing so isn't necessarily the greatest threat in the world.<br /> <br /> To the extent that I think the Tzimisce need to &quot;get past&quot; Vicissitude, it's not that I think Vicissitude is bad or that they need to abandon it. Rather, it's the opinion that over-specialization in a single Discipline limits possibilities. And, as I've noted before, one of the things that I like the most about the Path of Metamorphosis is that each individual's Path is going to be somewhat unique, and what Azhi Dahaka would be for them would be unique as well. Trying to argue that there is one &quot;right&quot; or &quot;orthodox&quot; way to approach the goal of Metamorphosis, to me, strips it of the most beautiful parts of its philosophy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25408_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25408\" data-vbnamecard=\"25408\">Alphari</a> My initial response when I first woke up was a bit unfairly hostile, so I'm going to remove it, apologize, and offer a better reply.<br /> <br /> I agree that the vast majority of Metamorphosists are Tzimisce that focus on the use of Vicissitude to achieve their goal. And I agree that Vicissitude was the inspiration for the philosophy, and that it has an important place in the tradition of the Path. I do not want to remove Vicissitude from the centre of the Metamorphosist movement, in the Dark Medieval or the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> As I have noted above, I believe that the philosophies of Metamorphosis are extremely flexible and variable in interpretation, and I believe that to be an opinion backed up in the text. While the majority of Metamorphosists likely are Tzimisce wielding Vicissitude, I think trying to exclude other forms of transformation simply because Vicissitude was &quot;the original&quot; is narrow-minded. And, to be fair, part of why I agree that the majority of Metamorphosists are still Vicissitude-wielding Tzimisce is because narrow-minded hubris is one of the most common flaws among the clan, and neither the clan nor members of the Path are the sort to go proselytizing it to others. But a highly individualistic Path is going to produce a diversity of interpretations, expressions, and deviations.<br /> <br /> That is what I am referring to when I talk about others being &quot;influenced&quot; by Metamorphosist philosophy. To use my example of a more Humane Metamorphosist, all you need to do is alter one premise of Tzimisce ego and Metamorphosist philosophy; that the former Humanity of the Vampire is not some absolutely inferior past state to be moved beyond, but is instead a necessary half of a synthesis that will produce a higher state of being if achieved.<br /> <br /> Similarly, while I have yet to read Constantinople By Night, it seems to me that the philosophy of the Divinity Within is at least somewhat influenced by exposure to the Metamorphosist traditions of the Tzimisce, given its preoccupation with Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;influenced,&quot; I merely mean that the ideas within it may have provoked thoughts leading to new ideas that can be traced back to Metamorphosist concepts, even if the Metamorphosists might disagree with what has been done with their philosophy. It happens in the real world all the time.<br /> <br /> So, again, to be very clear: <b>I agree that the vast majority of Metamorphosists are Tzimisce, and that they focus on Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> I do not think it is ALWAYS true. And therefore, I do not consider it invalid for other perspectives to be discussed. I do not think it is an attack on Vicissitude to consider other ideas.</b><br /> <br /> But to be clear:<br /> 1) the idea that Disciplines other than Vicissitude can have significant value to the Path of Metamorphosis is an implicit premise of this thread<br /> 2) continuing to argue against that position will be taken as derailment<br /> 3) If you want to continue this conversation in another thread, I will promise to make at least one response if you want to @ me to continue the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 11-10-2020, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T10:38:57-08:00","id":1422923,"title":"","content":"As you wish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Though in post <b>#23</b> I DID give you Disciplines that'd contribute to the Metamorphosis philosophy. It's just that they'd be more Physical style Disciplines than Blood Magic however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-10-2020, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T11:24:16-08:00","id":1422926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422746-tzimisce-metamorphosis-and-blood-magic?p=1422923#post1422923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you wish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Though in post <b>#23</b> I DID give you Disciplines that'd contribute to the Metamorphosis philosophy. It's just that they'd be more Physical style Disciplines than Blood Magic however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but my introduction also premises that you should bring up stuff not already discussed in the previously-linked thread, and that you should actually be discussing their value in detail. Just listing them off so you can spend the rest of your post arguing with the premise is still derailment. And Animalism and Auspex produce mental/spiritual changes, not physical ones, AFAIK?<br /> <br /> But yes, I 100% agree about all the physical Disciplines, 200% on Protean (who DOESN'T want Agg-claws for their Zulo-form?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T18:55:59-08:00","id":1423009,"title":"","content":"These are the Ethics for the V20 DAV Road:<br /> <br /> Discovering knowledge for oneself is the truest, purest form of understanding and the key to Metamorphosis.<br /> \u2022 Seek to understand life and death, for it is the cycle that bars transcendence.<br /> \u2022 Indulge the Beast and deny it; like all things, it must be understood.<br /> \u2022 Experiment endlessly, especially upon your own body, to reveal every secret at hand.<br /> \u2022 Do not divorce yourself from the world, for it is what you seek to understand, but do not allow yourself to be dragged down by its entanglements.<br /> <br /> Other than indulging the Beast, none of these Ethics would present major problems for Humanity. It would just be a different approach than if you followed the Road/Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T19:44:17-08:00","id":1423014,"title":"","content":"As you've noted, &quot;indulging the Beast&quot; is obviously a problem for Humanity, but you're also ignoring a lot of what is insinuated by &quot;Do not divorce yourself from the world... but do not allow yourself to be dragged down by its entanglements.&quot; It's pretty vague, but generally what's included in that are finnicky little things like &quot;human rights&quot; and &quot;being attached more to this person than all the interesting stuff you can learn by vivisecting them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've generally considered two &quot;variants&quot; to the &quot;orthodox&quot; Road of Metamorphosis:<br /> <br /> One is the more &quot;rationalist&quot; approach that takes Conviction, but not Instinct, and takes a lot from the Road of Bones/Path of Death and the Soul. Just focused more specifically on using all that knowledge for personal Metamorphosis; basically Sascha Vykos.<br /> <br /> The other is the more &quot;humanist&quot; approach that I discussed above. Rather than seeing Vampirism as an inherently superior condition, and Humanity something to be left behind, you instead view a synthesis of the best qualities of both as the Path to Metamorphosis. In an earlier post I mentioned using Vicissitude to hide among Humanity; not due to fear, but scientific curiosity, wanting to observe the subject (humanity) without disturbing it, &quot;in its natural environment.&quot; Or, taken a bit further, an interest in living the &quot;human experience&quot; as much as possible for a Vampire, for the purpose of expanding awareness and understanding. It was kinda inspired by this line from SWTOR, tbh, where the evil Emperor pursuing immortality (body-swap style) is asked what they could possibly want with it, and they respond that they'll just try every conceivable career or lifestyle, every possible experience. I found it interesting, and not just from a villainous perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T05:00:05-08:00","id":1423037,"title":"","content":"Interesting perspective. My take on that last Ethic was something like the Buddhist concept of attachment leading to suffering and the Christian one about being in the world, but not part of it.<br /> <br /> Another possible outlook could be a Harmonist approach. Under that Path, it mentions that as they progress, they come to understand their role is more like a parasite. I could see a Metamorphosist thinking, 'how do I transcend my parasitic state?'<br /> <br /> What is great about Metamorphosis is there is no single right answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T07:56:37-08:00","id":1423054,"title":"","content":"There is definitely an element of that Buddhist take there, I agree <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But you have to consider the parts in relation to one another, not just in isolation. And you need to consider the concepts and ethics of Buddhism that aren't present, as well. Mainstream Metamorphosis is a supremely egoistic endeavour, a belief that the Self exists and that it can become separate and superior to the Other Lesser Things. Buddhism believes in transcendence, but it also commonly believes that the Self is one of those illusions to transcend, which makes Metamorphosist acts that inflict suffering on Others for the sake of the Self to be an example of falling into the trap of attachment to this world.<br /> <br /> A Harmonist approach to Metamorphosis could definitely make for an interested hermit-mystic type character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I agree that the variety of ways to approach Azhi Dahaka is one of the most interesting parts of the Path <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}